# Repair Action Assignment & Labor Recognition

**Doctrine:** [docs/operations/repair-action-assignment-and-labor-recognition-v1.md](../../docs/operations/repair-action-assignment-and-labor-recognition-v1.md)

**Repair Orders organize customer work. Repair Actions organize technician work.**

## Two questions

| Authority | Question |
| --- | --- |
| **Repair Action Assignment** | Who owns this package? (`RepairActionOwner`) |
| **Labor Recognition** | Which labor lines are already paid as flag? |

## Hard invariants

- **`RepairActionOwner`** = accountable party (today: Technician only — not bare `owner_technician_id` forever)
- **Exactly one owner**; ownership **transfers**, never copies
- Collaborate → **split Repair Actions**; helper time → **R4**
- **Technician never receives an RO** — receives **owned Repair Actions**
- **Completed by** = current owner — not last labor-line touch
- Package Complete ≠ labor-only
- Recognition once per labor line; attribution from owner at R3

## R1 objective

First unit of shop work that belongs to a technician — **not** “assign technicians” on ROs.

## R1.1 — Operational communication

Repair Actions communicate technician progress: **Owner · Status · Latest Update · Updated At**.

Label is **Update** — not “Technician Notes” / not a historical log. One replaceable note. No chat.

RO `assigned_technician_id` is transitional compatibility only (seed/default). Do not read it for production meaning.

## Resume order

R0 ✅ → R1 ✅ → **R1.1 Status + Latest Update** → Observation locked → R2 only if earned → R3 recognition only after observation → R4 assists → R5 observe

During observation: no Labor Recognition, payroll, assists, Financial (RED), or redesign without verified defect.

Financial stays RED. Do not couple.
